  <title>ATF temperature sensor 1 curve</title>
  <description>[CONFIRMED, TCM 08 §5] Converts the filtered inverted sensor voltage (3FB792/793 = 255 − 3FB77B/77C) into the ATF temperature 3FB794 (id 110B) that every ATF-temp threshold in this calibration uses (cold 4→5 inhibit 0x606D6, P17xx debounce 0x4B0AD, lift-foot minimum 0x606E9, line-pressure ATF factor 0x60534). CONFIRMED live: 3FB77B 47 → 3FB792 207 → 3FB794 132 = this curve. FSM reference ATF TEMP SE 1: 2.2 V at 0 °C, 1.8 V at 20 °C, 0.6 V at 80 °C → curve ≈ 88 / 100 / 151. So the "cold" thresholds near 45-55 raw are well below 0 °C. Note: the K-line id reads about 18 lower than 3FB794 at the same voltage (conversion not found); use the RAM value with this curve.</description>
