  <description>[STRONG, TCM 04 §2] Sequencer B (3FB7D9, FUN_401A8): each phase lasts the tick count of the turbine-torque column, or ends early once shift progress 3FB2FC passes column 0 (upshift: progress &gt; col 0; downshift: &lt; col 0). Phase 1 adds the learned offset 3FB3D2; phase 2 of an upshift adds 3FB54A and is at least 0x6883E[shift]. A/B = the two element sequencers. On upshifts A (3FB502) is the engaging-element apply command: it starts at the initial-apply table and climbs by 3FB3D4 per step while B holds 10000, then jumps to 10000 when the shift completes; on coast downshifts B ramps while A holds (CONFIRMED live 2026-11-19, TCM 06). 1 tick = 20 ms: the sequencers run in the 20 ms task T44 (schedule table 0x10C00, CONFIRMED; live ramp steps every ~20-25 ms, TCM 06 §1).</description>
  <CATEGORYMEM index="0" category="5" />
  <XDFAXIS id="x" uniqueid="0x0">
    <EMBEDDEDDATA mmedelementsizebits="16" mmedmajorstridebits="-32" mmedminorstridebits="0" />
