<XDFCONSTANT uniqueid="0x11F5" flags="0x0">
  <title>Apply ramp steps 3→4, T ≤ 1000, speed ≤ max</title>
  <description>[STRONG, TCM 04 §3] Number of ticks the engaging-element pressure takes to ramp from its start to the target (3FB3E0 = (target − start) / steps, FUN_41B88/41C28). Fewer steps = steeper ramp = firmer, shorter shift. One step per 20 ms (task T44). The adaptive cell would scale the ramp, but the stock clamp holds it at 256 (TCM 06 §3). Table 0x629D4 (alt 0x62A38 when 3FB187 b2 = continuous same-direction shift, TCM 05 §3). Speed = processed vehicle speed 3FB797, km/h.</description>
